#
# Counter-example for math:SlotIndexUniquenessShape via a tensor computation node:
# the tensor node reuses the expression AST wholesale, so two math:argumentSlot cells
# sharing math:slotIndex 0 trip the SAME inherited uniqueness gate that guards every
# application/binder — proving the AST is reused, not forked. Each slot is otherwise
# well-formed, isolating the SPARQL uniqueness violation. Validation MUST emit
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:DuplicateArgumentSlotIndex).
# Bound by ex:ecTensorNodeDuplicateSlotIndex.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:badTensorNode a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator math:matrixProduct ;
    math:tensorOperation math:matrixProduct ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:dupSlotA , ex:dupSlotB .

ex:dupSlotA a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:tExprA .
ex:dupSlotB a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:tExprB .

ex:tExprA a math:MathematicalExpression .
ex:tExprB a math:MathematicalExpression .
